course: dictionary
lesson: 3157
title: Emergent: the top of the rainforest
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Emergent means starting to appear, grow or become known. You can often work it out from the words around it. «A few giant emergent trees poke out at the very top» tells you the emergent trees are above everything else.
explain: Think of a rainforest as a tower of homes in layers. The forest floor is at the bottom, then the dim understorey, then the canopy, a thick roof of leaves. The emergent layer is above that roof. «The emergent trees stick up above the canopy» shows they are the tallest.
explain: The word works the same way in other places. A pond plant that is emergent grows in the water, but its top sticks out of the water, like a reed. «Emergent readers» are children who are just starting to read. Swap in "just starting to grow" and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Emergent means starting to appear, grow or become known.
fact: The emergent layer is the very top of a rainforest, where the tallest trees poke above the canopy.
fact: From the top down, the rainforest layers are: emergent layer, canopy, understorey, forest floor.
fact: The canopy is the thick upper layer of leaves and branches, about 30 to 45 metres above the ground.
fact: «Emergent readers» are children who are just starting to read.
exercise: In a rainforest, which layer is the very top? | *Emergent layer | Canopy | Understorey | Forest floor
exercise: «Emergent readers are children just starting to read.» What does emergent mean here? | Very old and wise | Lost in a dark forest | *Just starting to appear or grow | Finished and complete
exercise: Which layer sits between the emergent layer and the understorey? | *Canopy | Forest floor | Grassy field | Dark cave
test: An emergent plant grows in a pond, but its top sticks up out of the water. Which plant is it like? | *Reed | Lily pad | Seaweed | Coral
test: Which layer is the thick roof of leaves, about 30 to 45 metres up? | Understorey | *Canopy | Forest floor | Emergent layer
exam: Jayden says emergent means the same as ancient. Which meaning is right? | Dark and quiet | *Starting to appear or grow, like the trees that poke up above the canopy | Old and ancient | Heavy and slow
